{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1012694-mystery-questions","id":1012694,"title":"Mystery questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-05T11:37:57-08:00","id":1012694,"title":"Mystery questions","content":"Assuming I\u2019m not using a crossover Mystery, nor am I using a mage\u2019s Awakened magic as a mystery:<br /> <br /> <br /> Surface information: My basic understanding is that I give age and what practice the mystery in question most closely resembles. There doesn\u2019t seem to be anything else listed here; so I\u2019m not sure what else would be given as surface info.<br /> <br /> <br /> Deep Information: \u2018Identification of the phenomenon as being linked to one the mage has Scrutinized before\u2019 doesn\u2019t make sense to me -- assuming that the Mage has been given a reason to study this in the first place, wouldn\u2019t this one be obvious? Or is this more for that moment of \u201cI was pretty certain we were dealing with the Croatoan virus from a few months ago; but honestly this is looking more like some sort of hedge-curse?\u201d Am I missing something? I feel like the links to previous phenomenon should be\u2026 obvious before scrutiny, most of the time. Right?<br /> <br /> I\u2019m also uncertain how power levels relative to mage\u2019s gnosis should go for non-crossover, non-awakened mysteries. <br /> <br /> <br /> \u2018How the Arcanum used relates to the Mystery\u2019 makes no sense to me, either. The only examples they give are crossover material; and even with my understanding of the crossovers they use, I\u2019m not certain I track what the intention is here. \u201cDeep information about the undead blood in the ghoul\u201d specifically means very little to me, because while they\u2019ve told me what the information is about, they haven\u2019t told me what the information itself is. Revealing that a changeling\u2019s powers are contractually born does, kinda. That information is tied up in the origin or \u2018supernatural mechanics\u2019 of the power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T11:58:46-08:00","id":1012707,"title":"","content":"For a non-Awakened magic mystery, I would give out the age of the mystery, the practice it resembles, and the most obvious arcana that cover the domain of the mystery.<br /> <br /> For your question re: deep information, I think the certainty of it is really what's at debate. I agree that it should be obvious that two similar phenomena <i>could be</i> linked, I think deep information verifies whether that link is true or simply spurious. For example, two people killed in the same manner using the Forces arcana could simply be coincidence. I think gathering Deep Information would reveal that it is not actually coincidental and the two are actually connected.<br /> <br /> As for how the arcanum used relates to the mystery, I think that's the most straightforward one, right? How does the substance of the Mystery relate to the domain of the arcana? Most of the time this is going to be easy. Ashes in the wastebin? Result of magical fire via Forces. Really unlikely car accident? Result of probability tampering via Fate. I think the examples given are for crossovers because that's where this gets less obvious. In the case of the ghoul, if the mystery is *what is this creature* then knowing that it's alive but with undead blood in it is certainly a step in the right direction.<br /> <br /> Do you have a specific Mystery in mind that you'd like to flesh out?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I'm an idiot and missed the first line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My ideas are bad and I should feel bad.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12157-kvark","name":"Kvark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"186"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-06T16:24:52-08:00","id":1013466,"title":"","content":"Good questions.<br /> <br /> I interpreted the deep scrutiny links as details like the same caster or type of supernatural phenomena, so very much like &quot;Wait, this has similarities to a spirit I dealt with last year... but why?&quot; rather than &quot;Oh, a spirit of murder was created by the Origami Murderer and that must have Influenced this killer.&quot; or anything that precise. I agree, though, that a bit more clarity on that would help. Examples of a number of different sorts would, especially.<br /> <br /> I would run supernatural stuff using Rank as the power stat. for ephemera and half (truncating) of the merit rating for any purely merit-based power as the power stat. for that. Mostly, this is simply because that feels about right and not because I know of any rule that specifies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}